acceptance/test_assign_depots.py has two tests that contradict each other for the same input:

- test_nearest_depot: assign_depots(NET, ["D1","D2"], ["ISO","D1"]) == {"ISO": None, "D1": "D1"}
- test_regression_issue_233: assign_depots(NET, ["D1","D2"], ["ISO","D1"]) == {"D1": "D1"}

Both use the identical input (ISO is an unreachable non-depot customer). One expects the unreachable customer to map to None, the other expects it to be omitted entirely. They cannot both pass.

The docstring spec says 'Returns a dict that maps every customer code to the code of its nearest depot, or to None if no depot can reach the customer', so the docstring-correct behavior is to include {"ISO": None} (i.e. test_nearest_depot is correct, test_regression_issue_233 is the buggy one).

Please confirm which is the source of truth and fix the test so the correct one can merge.

